# Go renderer internals

## Package roles

| Package | Responsibility |
|---------|----------------|
| `pdf` | Objects, lexer/parser, xref/repair, decrypt, page tree |
| `filter` | Stream decode + predictors |
| `graphics` | Matrices, rects, paths, colorspaces, pixmaps |
| `font` | Embedded fonts, encodings, ToUnicode, base-14 |
| `content` | Content-stream interpreter, images, HTML assembly |
| `render` | `Device`, `DrawDevice` (PNG), `HTMLDevice` (SVG/HTML) |

## Device seam

`content` must call rendering only through `render.Device`.

```
interpreter → Device.FillPath / StrokePath / FillText / FillImage / …
                ├─ DrawDevice → raster → PNG
                └─ HTMLDevice → SVG fragments → document.html
```

- Do not bypass `Device` with direct raster or SVG writes from `content`
- Prefer extending `BaseDevice` / existing devices over new parallel pipelines
- Do not casually rewrite the scanline rasterizer, stroker, or flatten path

## Change hygiene

- Touch the smallest package that owns the bug
- Match existing style; run `gofmt`
- Pair behavior changes with tests in the owning package when practical
